 not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T18:11:08-07:00","id":207765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/207354-emperor-for-a-day?p=207723#post207723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And now we've killed the mood. DAMNIT!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm still in the mood. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In that spirit, we shall now dance the Dance of Brotherly Love! Mamushka!<br /> <img src=\"http://ghostgirlsto.files.wordpress.com/2012/10/the_addams_family_8746_medium.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T18:46:43-07:00","id":207794,"title":"","content":"Very well then!<br /> <br /> If I were made Emperor, I would make law that all major conflicts would be resolved by combat between giant robots, controlled by the best and brightest of each nation and appropriately themed for the culture from which they come.<br /> <br /> I would also replace all sports with competitive robot/powersuit wargames.<br /> <br /> All law enforcement officials would be required to wear color-coordinated uniforms, and learn synchronized martial arts.<br /> <br /> I have absolutely no doubt this would produce an objectively better world by the end of the week. (Surely)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T19:20:43-07:00","id":207808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/207354-emperor-for-a-day?p=207794#post207794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very well then!<br /> <br /> If I were made Emperor, I would make law that all major conflicts would be resolved by combat between giant robots, controlled by the best and brightest of each nation and appropriately themed for the culture from which they come.<br /> <br /> I would also replace all sports with competitive robot/powersuit wargames.<br /> <br /> All law enforcement officials would be required to wear color-coordinated uniforms, and learn synchronized martial arts.<br /> <br /> I have absolutely no doubt this would produce an objectively better world by the end of the week. (Surely)</div> </div> </div> </div>So much yes.<br /> <br /> EDIT: SO MUCH","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T20:37:17-07:00","id":207858,"title":"","content":"Balkanize the shit out of Russia and China. For laughs, give a few bits to Ukraine.<br /> <br /> Reunite Czechoslovakia. And maybe North and South Korea after Kim Jung Un is deposed. Break ISIS. While we're at it, lets stabilize the Middle East and make Israel stop being our psychotic ally. Bringing down Hamas and his cronies should help with that of course. Outlaw any governments ability to arrest a journalist for journalism the world over. Yes Egypt that means you've got to play nice with Al Jeezera or however you spell it.<br /> <br /> It occurs to me a lot of this cannot be done in 24 hours. And at least half of it would probably result in something horrible. But, I like to think it says good things about me that given the choice, I'd like to live in a world that's less insane than the one I'm in now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T20:48:37-07:00","id":207876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/207354-emperor-for-a-day?p=207858#post207858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Reunite] North and South Korea after Kim Jung Un is deposed. Break ISIS. While we're at it, lets stabilize the Middle East and make Israel stop being our psychotic ally. Bringing down Hamas and his cronies should help with that of course. Outlaw any government's ability to arrest a journalist for journalism the world over.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of these are excellent ideas. Or, well, I don't know how much North and South Korea want to be united, but Kim Jong-Un needs to be deposed immediately, and the entire regime overthrown. Reuniting them seems like a good way to sweep up the pieces, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T23:16:59-07:00","id":207939,"title":"","content":"I would get somebody to replace the battery on my mac. I think it's worn out and a little slow now. I would also safeguard the future of the Last Escape trilogy and dismantle the prison industrial complex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T23:40:23-07:00","id":207959,"title":"","content":"Can I cheat? Specifically, can I issue a mandate redefining the meaning of &quot;hour&quot; in my domain (&quot;Earth, the International Space Station, All Manmade Orbital Objects and the Moon&quot;) so I'm emperor for long enough to actually get a lot of shit done? Or more simply, abuse &quot;Anything you decide during those 24 hours cannot be undone by the various nation-states and corporations that return to power after the 24 hours are up&quot; to have one of my decisions be &quot;after my 24 hours as Emperor are done, I get to keep all the power I had during that time&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T00:56:49-07:00","id":207987,"title":"","content":"I would fullfill my lifelong dream and have scientists genetically engineer a cyber-raptor from a chicken. I will name him Tray and he will be my best friend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1266-sirpants","name":"SirPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T06:08:12-07:00","id":208209,"title":"","content":"Well, I can't make moves about other nations since I don't know enough about them, but I'm tired of seeing the US reliving the late 19th century. <br /> <br /> <u><i>Trade</i></u><br /> Global trade was promoted on the basis that everyone would benefit, importing nations and exporting nations alike. But true reciprocity hasn't happened. America's competitors learned long ago that America pretty much is a wuss when getting tough on trade. They lowered their tariffs but raised other barriers to block entry on US products into their markets. Washington's response, as its been for decades, was to continue to negotiate agreements with individual countries that promise to open their markets, yet never do, at least not to the extent the US does. (The story of US/Japan relations and now we see a repeat performance with China.)<br /> Government's emphasis needs to be changed from exports to imports, at least until trade is brought into balance. That means controls need to be placed on imported goods. In other words, access to the world's richest consumer market should be granted on the basis of national interest, not because of a blind adherence to an abstract concept like &quot;free trade.&quot;<br /> This is especially true when one considers that so-called &quot;free trade&quot; has never existed in all of recorded history. Every nation has imposed controls on the flow of goods across its borders, in its own self-interest. The US has come closer than any other nation to the free - trade concept, all at the expense of working Americans.<br /> <br /> <u><i>Immigration</i></u><br /> Restore immigration to pre - 1990 levels and scale back the skilled - worker and guest - worker visa programs that have led to widespread abuses in employment - based immigration. The practice of using immigration policy to create a labor surplus, thereby helping to hold down wages or limit wage increases, should be ended. (Re: US Commission on Immigration reform headed by Barbara Jordan.)<br /> <br /> <u><i>Global Wages</i></u><br /> Companies that produce goods in foreign countries to take advantage of cheap labor should not be permitted to dictate the wages paid to American workers.<br /> A solution: Impose a tariff on goods brought into the country equal to the wage differential between foreign workers and US workers in the same industry. That way, competition would be confined to who makes the best product, not who works for the least amount of money.<br /> <br /> <u><i>Taxes</i></u> <br /> (Oh boy!!!)<br /> Reestablish the progressive income tax, which rests on the principle that tax rates rise with income. This structure was in place from the beginning of WWII until the early 60s. <br /> Point of history that no one seems to have learned (and libertarians refuse to): No taxpayer has ever paid out 91% of their income in taxes during the aforementioned timeframe. The max rate of 91% was applied only to taxable income over $400,000. Adjusted today that would be almost $5 million. (I imagine anyone making that kind of money might be able to eke out a meager existence if he/she budgets well enough.)<br /> To further simplfy the system, all deductions should be eliminated. So too the preferential capital gains tax. All dollars would be treated alike. A middle class family whose income is derived solely from a paycheck would not be taxed at a higher effective rate than someone whose income is derived from speculating on Wall Street.<br /> Now that was federal income tax. State and local taxes tend to weigh even more on the middle class and lower income workers. To right this, the federal government could create a system of rewards and penalties when distributing revenue-sharing money to the states. The more progressive a state's tax structure, the more federal aid it would receive.<br /> And then there is corporate income tax.<br /> With sharply lower rates and a variety of tax concessions, corporations today pay less income tax than corporations 50 years ago. Back then, corporations accounted for 39% of all income tax revenue; individuals supplied 61%. Currently the corporate share is below the 19% mark while the individual share rose to over 81%.<br /> To restore some measure of balance, the top corporate tax rate should at least be raised above the highest personal rate of 39.6%. In the 1950s, it was 52%. By 1996, it was 35%. A variey of corporate deductions should be eliminated or scaled back. these include the essentially unlimited deduction for interest payments and the carryover deduction of losses, both of which fuel mergers and takeovers. Also foreign tax provisions need to be amended so that multinational companies no longer would be able to move income around the world to escape payment of taxes.<br /> <br /> <u><i>Government Regulations</i></u><br /> Keep the good and toss the bad...<br /> We must preserve the rules that assure the quality of American life: the food you eat, the medicines you take, the air you breathe and the water you drink.<br /> US businesses must spend money to comply with these regulations, while their competitors in foreign countries are spared that expense. Whether the competitors are American-owned or foreign-owned doesn't matter; the results are an uneven playing field. One way to remedy this is to impose a tariff on imported products equal to the amount of money that American businesses must spend to comply with government regulations.<br /> <br /> <u><i>Executive Salaries</i></u><br /> Corporations are free to pay their executives whatever they want. But that doesn't mean companies should be permitted to write off the full salary amount on their tax returns, thereby shifting the cost to taxpayers.<br /> Possible solution: The tax deductibility to a multiple between the highest and lowest paid workers. For example, if the lowest paid worker earns $20k, then the company would be precluded from deducting more than say, 15x that amount, or $300k. While the company could pay its top officer any amount, only $300k could be written off on the corporate tax return. The balance would come out of the shareholders' pockets, rather than the taxpayers' pockets.<br /> <br /> <u><i>Campaign Finance and Lobby Reform</i></u> (The first and foremost thing that needs to be done)<br /> Absent sweeping reforms in capaign financing, all other reform efforts are likely to fail.<br /> Tens of millions of dollars from corporations, wealthy individuals, political action committees (PACs), and other interest groups, all with agendas that often are at odds with what is good for the average American. (The last presidential campaign cost nearly $1 billion. That's just wrong.)<br /> Campaign contributions not only elect candidates, but they give the donors access to the lawmakers after they are in office. That's another benefit beyond the reach of average Americans.<br /> Impose a limit on the amount of money that can be spent to run for office.<br /> Ban contributions by political action committees to political candidates.<br /> Close any loophole in current campaign finance law that allows wealthy individuals and corporations to circumvent limits on contributions to political candidates by making contributions in any amount to political parties.<br /> Place restrictions on the amount of out-of-state money a congressional candidate can accept while running for office.<br /> -----------------------<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key