014, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T07:13:17-07:00","id":208278,"title":"","content":"I don't know much else that I would do, just because this one things is on my mind.<br /> <br /> Being the liberal/hippie/socialist that I am, I'd impose a restriction upon the discrepancy between what the average worker is paid versus the average (useless) executive.<br /> <br /> In most developed countries, the average executive gets between 15 and 25 times what the average worker does. In America and other underdeveloped countries, it can be as high and 350 times more. Time for a cap on that. I think 30 times is more than enough. The excess goes to hiring more workers at higher wages, thus allowing the economy to grow by putting more of the money in circulation, instead of 1% sitting on it and spending way too much of it on things that aren't necessary (gold-plated toilets) or things that don't really exist (stock futures).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T08:01:09-07:00","id":208