f-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T13:14:13-07:00","id":208592,"title":"","content":"Papa Bear, why?<br /> <br /> A negative income tax fueled by excess profits of corporations would be so much more simple, you'd be encouraging the business to expand while also laying seed corn for the rise of new business by lifting up the bottom. This system from where I'm standing sounds like it'd play merry havoc with the business cycle causing a lot of already existent problems to get worse; most notably the horrible tendency of first world corporations to go through cancerous and unsustainable growth at the first sign of success, and ultimately encourage the rise of monopoly and capito-feudalism","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1266-sirpants","name":"SirPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T14:06:49-07:00","id":208664,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of things I would want to do, but inspite of space bats cool enough to help me enact them I know they would fail. Assuming that this could all be done without crashing and burning? Things like a global democratic government(and one that would actually work and no fucking lobbyists that can push agendas by buying the politicians). In turn a global government would then allow the helping of those people or nations that either can't be helped correctly or that to do so would just bleed a single country to death. If resources can travel more freely then maybe some good could actually be done. A single unified military and constabulary that could stop gorilla elements, pirates, gangs/mobs/etc, shutdown human trafficking/slavery/etc, or prevent the rise of dictators/despots/etc(even if you bring about world peace today there is always tomorrow). All of which cannot then be used to become a military state/big brother/etc. Governments cannot steal &quot;borrow&quot; funds from other programs for expediency(no more stealing from Peter to pay Paul).<br /> <br /> I could go on and on so lets make the rest key points instead.<br /> <br /> * CEOs of companies cannot bleed it dry, get government assistance, and then bleed that dry before flying off to sun in Bermuda.<br /> * Technology cannot be hindered simply because the status quo is making more money and because future tech conserves instead which ultimately means less money.<br /> * Fix the actual issues with people and health care and don't just say everyone foot the bill for everyone instead of fixing actual issues.<br /> * Rewriting of many laws because more that a few times the law or precedent the law is based on has been enacted by an idiot that shouldn't have been allow to feed themselves let alone make a legal decision. A pet peeve example.<br /> * An equitable way to determine frivolous lawsuits and then such lawsuits are punished by the paying of all salaries involved by both the individual and their representation. Personal stupidity should never be finagled into grounds to sue someone.<br /> * Lawsuits that have actual grounds the sued party(including representation) then also has to pay not only the monies awarded, but also the full costs incurred by the court for said trial. When paying someone off doesn't work then bogging down the system to prevent having to pay shouldn't be an option.<br /> Because maybe if everyone has to foot the total bill for their stupidity they will think more than twice about doing it in the first place.<br /> <br /> Even by bullet points this could go on and on. There is 